{"base_commit":"1b060ef01d1504ec856cb65fb3fdab30c63f001a","behavioral_test_evidence":true,"candidate_id":"quality-candidate:v1:6fca2ccc287f8d3ccd407100bca2a8b154ae61ef8ed5e5442c520af33ac33271","candidate_status":"deferred_for_review","changed_file_count":2,"changed_files":[{"additions":2,"change_type":"MODIFIED","deletions":4,"is_test":false,"path":"aten/src/ATen/native/Onehot.cpp"},{"additions":1,"change_type":"MODIFIED","deletions":5,"is_test":true,"path":"test/test_nn.py"}],"content_hash":"sha256:006a0c54facc54f0f010eac52c9d7626b2485e86c70e0882199ba67cc90f5591","contract_type":"quality_candidate","created_at":"2026-07-29T00:00:00Z","description":"Fixes https://github.com/intel/torch-xpu-ops/issues/3284\r\n\r\nCurrently OneHot has boundary checks for CPU and these checks are skipped for `CUDA`, `MPS`, `XLA` and `PrivateUser1`. As `XPU` is not included on the list it causes D2H calls that affect performance.\r\n\r\nInstead of adding `XPU` to the list I think it's better to flip the condition to check boundaries only for `CPU` and allow accelerators to skip this validation.","execution_hints":{"devices":["cpu","cuda"],"distributed":false,"modes":["eager"],"phases":["forward"]},"linked_issues":[],"merge_commit":"90bf988d397a2a2be6079aeeec50d870c3f28146","merged_at":"2026-04-23T21:09:23Z","pr_number":181211,"pr_url":"https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/pull/181211","proposed_contract_families":["efficiency_safety"],"proposed_trigger_tags":["device_specific"],"repository":"pytorch/pytorch","required_hardware":["cpu","cuda"],"runtime_supported":true,"schema_version":"v1","source_available":true,"title":"Split onehot checks for CPU and accelerators"}